### Screenshots, recordings, and evidence

No screenshots attached. The generic server and deterministic tests contain no personal or financial data. Local browser captures and per-session predicate summaries were retained privately.

### Impact and severity

Intermittent embedded-app failure for non-admin users. The assistant can finish its text reply while its app card is unavailable. One earlier two-chat control had one captured failure. The fixed-size comparison below did not reproduce it naturally, so it does not establish a failure-rate improvement.

### Proposed fix

In `dist/mcp-app-CHXbi1_o.mjs`, change only the two retention calls:

- Line 116, `mcp.app.view`: `retainSessionScopedRead(options, sessionKey, agentId, { allowMetadataChanges: true })`.
- Line 72, `operationHandler` for active-view tool/resource operations: add the same fourth argument. This is an operation read, not a separate lease endpoint.

The diff is below. No change to `session-utils-read-lifetime` or publication settlement is proposed.

| Trial | Missing-session errors |
| --- | ---: |
| Unpatched, new status-server revision, six NEW chats | 0/6 |
| Access-only patch, same server/config/model, six NEW chats | 0/6 |
| Deterministic unsettled metadata postimage, strict matcher | rejected |
| Same deterministic postimage, access-only matcher | accepted |

Every browser trial sent exactly `how are we doing?`. Each `mcp.app.view` logged a non-skipped read and successful row predicates in these twelve trials. **The 0/6 versus 0/6 comparison does not prove that the intermittent browser failure is eliminated.** The deterministic test proves the narrower proposed mechanism handles a known, unsettled metadata postimage.

Why no wait is needed for that case: `predicatePending` already calls `predicate.matches(entryPostimage)`. The access-only callback from `retainSessionScopedRead` checks `hasSessionReadAccessChanged`, while `retainGatewaySessionEntryReadOnly` still requires the same session ID and lifecycle revision. The strict matcher rejects harmless postimages; the access-only matcher accepts them even before settlement.

The seven deterministic checks cover metadata acceptance, rejection of an unknown pending publication, and rejection of pending session reset, lifecycle replacement, creator change, visibility change and incognito change. Unknown pending writes remain blocked. The patch leaves requester, scope, role, routing, physical-store, view, tool and resource authorization checks intact; it does not bypass access checks or authorize writes.

### Additional information

An AI coding agent found and reproduced the missing-session failure on a local bench, ran the comparison and deterministic tests, and drafted this report. I approved filing it.

Merged #162681 is related precedent for access-only retained reads during approval replay, not a duplicate of this MCP Apps issue. I make no claim about an earlier OpenClaw version working.

