## TUI: scroll position jumps to the top when a reply finishes (scrollback cleared on content redraw), with a working patch

This is still reproducible on **OpenClaw 2026.11.3** (bundled `@earendil-works/pi-tui` **1.0.3**), Linux, VTE-based terminal (Ptyxis / GNOME Terminal). It continues #114600 and #44130, which were closed by the bots as duplicate and then as stale; their instruction was to open a new issue if it still happens.

### What happens
If you scroll up to read while a reply streams or finishes, the view jumps back to the top or bottom. Every forced full redraw in `tui-main-screen.js` writes `ESC[2J ESC[H ESC[3J`. That clears the screen **and the terminal's scrollback**, so the reading position is lost. VTE also archives the viewport on ED2, so scrollback fills with repeated copies of the screen.

### The fix
A patch to `dist/tui-main-screen.js` in pi-tui 1.0.3 (diff below):
- A forced content refresh (`resetRenderState`) is no longer treated as a terminal resize. Geometry and history are kept; only an unchanged viewport is force-redrawn.
- A content-driven full redraw erases the visible rows one by one (`ESC[2K`) instead of ED2+ED3, and writes only the visible tail. Scrollback is not deleted, and no viewport copies pile up.
- **Real width changes keep the old behaviour** (`clear === "scrollback"`), because wrapping changes.

### Testing
- Synthetic frames run in a real off-screen GTK3 / VTE 0.84 terminal, with the scroll anchor set 40 rows up:
  - **unpatched:** FAIL. The anchor jumps 40 → 0 when the reply finishes;
  - **patched:** PASS on 56 stable-anchor transitions, including 50 appends, at both 75×25 and 120×32;
  - all 50 synthetic message markers appear exactly once in the buffer, and the older-history marker and a draft marker remain.
- These were synthetic messages in an off-screen VTE, not the live Ptyxis (GTK4) window.
- Separately, the patched file has been in daily use since 2026-11-10 on OpenClaw 2026.11.3, with no scroll snapback reported.

### Credit
Local adaptation, additional redraw fixes and VTE regression testing by **Hermes**, an AI agent on my team. It builds on **@joemcurry**'s scrollback-preservation proposal in earendil-works/pi#4204 (closed, not merged). The tail-only redraw and the `clear = true` / `"scrollback"` split, which keeps ED3 for width changes, come from that PR. If this lands, please credit both.

Because the code lives in pi-tui, the fix probably belongs upstream in earendil-works/pi, then a pi-tui version bump in OpenClaw. I'm filing here so the OpenClaw TUI issue has a working fix attached.

