### Summary

Add an optional `dreaming` provider to `MemoryPluginCapability` so the plugin that owns `plugins.slots.memory` can supply the phase status, promotion counters and operator actions the Control UI's Dreams tab shows, and have `doctor.memory.*` consult it before memory-core's bundled runtime.

### Problem to solve

The Memory page treats the memory slot owner as the engine, but the Dreams tab and the `doctor.memory.*` methods behind it are bound to memory-core's private internals (`createDoctorHandlers(memoryCoreRuntime = memory_core_bundled_runtime_exports)` in `src/gateway/server-methods/doctor.ts`). A third-party memory plugin can feed two of the page's five data sources through public surfaces and cannot reach the other three at all. Established by reading the 2026.9.1 bundle and by running a third-party slot owner against it:

