## What Problem This Solves

Microsoft Teams agent replies can load local attachments with process-wide media roots instead of the replying agent’s roots. A reply referencing another session’s sandbox file can therefore send that file.

## User Impact

Teams replies respect agent-scoped local media access. Allowed attachments continue to send; rejected attachments surface through the existing delivery error handling. No configuration migration is required.

## Why This Change Was Made

Pass the agent’s media roots and configured media access from the reply dispatcher into the existing outbound-media loader. This replaces the unscoped loader without adding another policy owner.

