## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: `reloadAndResume` fails after 60 seconds when other admitted work still holds the plugin being replaced.

## User Impact

Plugin reloads can finish and automatically resume the requesting conversation when existing work drains within the cancellable ten-minute wait budget. New agent runs wait behind the replacement gate during that drain. No configuration changes or migration are required. During this explicit maintenance handoff, new agent runs across the Gateway can wait for up to ten minutes of admitted-work draining; later cleanup/recovery keep their separate deadlines. Stop remains available.

## Why This Change Was Made

The requesting turn already releases its leases before the detached reload starts. Use the existing explicit-wait policy for that handoff so other admitted work also has time to finish.

**Policy proposal for maintainer review:** Treat the explicit `reloadAndResume` maintenance handoff like `reload --wait`. Ordinary `reload` requests still use their existing 60-second budget. This deliberately accepts a longer Gateway-wide admission delay for the handoff; it adds no unlimited wait, forced cancellation, retry, configuration option, or change to the existing rollback/cancellation owners. Approval of this policy is still for an upstream maintainer; no such approval is claimed.

