issues.body:
### Bug Description

When the assistant sends an attachment with a caption and then streams a separate answer in the same turn, the WebUI displays the attachment and caption but omits the entire follow-up answer. The turn still completes. History replay shows the same omission even when `stream_end.text` contains the full answer. The answer message is missing, not clipped within a message bubble.

The live event order is a regular assistant `message` with `media_urls`, followed by answer `delta` and `stream_end` events, then `turn_end`, all for the same turn. Removing only `media_urls` from the first message makes both messages appear.

### Steps to Reproduce

#### Deterministic WebUI test

1. Use a disposable source checkout of [v0.4.2](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/tree/v0.4.2) or the tested [`main` commit](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/commit/37c2af8ffc86c5adf0a9e42732e26722d8a4260b). The test requires Bun for dependency installation and Node.js for Vitest, but no Python gateway, model, credentials, or image file.
2. Save the fixture below as `webui/src/tests/repro-attachment-followup.test.tsx`. The live test feeds events through the real `NanobotClient` and `useNanobotStream` via a mock WebSocket. The history test passes the same turn to `ThreadTranscript.accept`, using a `stream_end` snapshot with the complete answer in place of the live `delta`.
3. From the checkout root, run:

   ```sh
   cd webui
   bun install --frozen-lockfile
   node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run src/tests/repro-attachment-followup.test.tsx --maxWorkers=1 --minWorkers=1
   ```

4. Both attachment cases fail. The only assistant message is `Diagram attached.` with `fixture.png`. Both controls pass: without `media_urls`, `The blue square marks the start of the route.` appears as a separate message after the caption.

<details>
<summary>Vitest reproduction fixture</summary>

```tsx
import { act, renderHook } from "@testing-library/react";
import type { ReactNode } from "react";
import { expect, it } from "vitest";
import { useNanobotStream } from "@/hooks/useNanobotStream";
import { ThreadTranscript } from "@/lib/thread-transcript";
import type { ThreadProjectionEvent, UIMessage } from "@/lib/types";
import { ClientProvider } from "@/providers/ClientProvider";
import { createStreamClient } from "./stream-client";

const chat_id = "fixture-chat";
const turn_id = "fixture-turn";
const stream_id = "fixture-stream:1";
const base = { chat_id, turn_id };
const text = "The blue square marks the start of the route.";
const caption = "Diagram attached.";
const image = { kind: "image" as const, url: "/fixture.png", name: "fixture.png" };

function events(withAttachment: boolean): ThreadProjectionEvent[] {
  return [
    { ...base, event: "user_message", turn_seq: 1, starts_turn: true, text: "Send a diagram, then explain it." },
    { ...base, event: "message", turn_seq: 2, text: caption, ...(withAttachment ? { media_urls: [image] } : {}) },
    { ...base, event: "delta", turn_seq: 3, stream_id, text },
    { ...base, event: "stream_end", turn_seq: 4, stream_id },
    { ...base, event: "turn_end", turn_seq: 5 },
  ];
}

function assistantRows(messages: UIMessage[]) {
  return messages.filter(({ role }) => role === "assistant").map(({ content, media }) => ({
    content, attachments: media?.map(({ name }) => name) ?? [],
  }));
}

const body = { content: text, attachments: [] };
const rows = (withAttachment: boolean) => [
  { content: caption, attachments: withAttachment ? [image.name] : [] }, body,
];

it.each([true, false])("live stream preserves the explanation (attachment=%s)", (withAttachment) => {
  const { client, receive } = createStreamClient();
  const wrapper = ({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) => (
    <ClientProvider client={client} token="" allowUpdateFlow={false}>{children}</ClientProvider>
  );
  const { result } = renderHook(() => useNanobotStream(chat_id), { wrapper });
  for (const event of events(withAttachment)) act(() => receive(event));
  expect(assistantRows(result.current.messages)).toEqual(rows(withAttachment));
});

it.each([true, false])("history replay preserves the explanation (attachment=%s)", (withAttachment) => {
  const thread = new ThreadTranscript();
  // Stored history contains the completed stream snapshot in place of the live delta.
  const persisted = events(withAttachment)
    .filter((event) => event.event !== "delta")
    .map((event) => event.event === "stream_end" ? { ...event, text, text_from_seq: 3 } : event);
  expect(thread.accept({ schemaVersion: 3, projection: "events", events: persisted,
    completed_turn_ids: [turn_id] }, thread.begin("initial"))).toBe(true);
  expect(assistantRows(thread.messages)).toEqual(rows(withAttachment));
});
```

</details>

#### Optional manual scenario (model-dependent)

In a new WebUI chat with a streaming model and the `message` tool available, ask the assistant to send a test image from the workspace to the current chat, then explain it in its normal answer rather than in another `message` call. For example: “Send `fixture.png` using the `message` tool with the caption ‘Diagram attached.’ After the tool returns, explain what the diagram shows in your final answer.” Check the live chat and then reopen the thread. This scenario only exercises the bug if the assistant actually streams a separate answer after sending the attachment.

### Expected Behavior

The WebUI should display the attachment and its caption, followed by the separate answer. The answer should be visible during live streaming and when the same turn is loaded from history.

### Relevant Logs

Vitest result summary for each tested source revision: 2 failed, 2 passed.

```shell
FAIL  live stream preserves the explanation (attachment=true)
FAIL  history replay preserves the explanation (attachment=true)
PASS  live stream preserves the explanation (attachment=false)
PASS  history replay preserves the explanation (attachment=false)

Expected assistant contents: ["Diagram attached.", "The blue square marks the start of the route."]
Actual with attachment:      ["Diagram attached."]
```

### nanobot Version

v0.4.2 source tag (`0dc8679edcc6061fbcdf3de13c7e16000e9d1b65`); `main` at `37c2af8ffc86c5adf0a9e42732e26722d8a4260b`

### Python Version

N/A — no gateway used in the deterministic test

### Operating System

Linux x86_64 (test runner)

### Channel / Platform

WebUI / WebSocket

### LLM Provider

N/A — synthetic events

### Model

N/A — synthetic events

### Browser

N/A — Vitest 2.1.9 with happy-dom 16.8.1 on Node.js 18.19.1

### Connection

Mock WebSocket for live events; in-memory history payload for replay

### Configuration (Optional)

_No response_

### Additional Context

#### Why the answer is omitted

- The gateway can emit an [assistant `message` carrying `media_urls`](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/blob/37c2af8ffc86c5adf0a9e42732e26722d8a4260b/nanobot/webui/outbound_delivery.py#L463-L490). In the [regular `message` branch](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/blob/37c2af8ffc86c5adf0a9e42732e26722d8a4260b/webui/src/lib/thread-event-projection.ts#L1159-L1209), the WebUI adds the attachment message and sets `suppressUntilTurnEnd` based on the presence of media, without establishing that later text would duplicate that message.
- While that flag is set, [`useNanobotStream` skips incoming answer deltas](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/blob/37c2af8ffc86c5adf0a9e42732e26722d8a4260b/webui/src/hooks/useNanobotStream.ts#L692-L731), and the [shared projector skips `delta` and returns early on `stream_end`](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/blob/37c2af8ffc86c5adf0a9e42732e26722d8a4260b/webui/src/lib/thread-event-projection.ts#L996-L1007), even if the latter contains the full answer. In this sequence, `turn_end` clears the flag but does not restore the skipped text.
- The [gateway can persist the full answer on `stream_end`](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/blob/37c2af8ffc86c5adf0a9e42732e26722d8a4260b/nanobot/webui/transcript.py#L336-L346) without storing individual deltas. [`ThreadTranscript` uses the same projector to replay history](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/blob/37c2af8ffc86c5adf0a9e42732e26722d8a4260b/webui/src/lib/thread-transcript.ts#L530-L550), so the answer can be present in the history payload but absent from the UI. The test demonstrates a display omission, not deletion from storage.

#### Regression scope

An [existing test](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/blob/37c2af8ffc86c5adf0a9e42732e26722d8a4260b/webui/src/tests/useNanobotStream.test.tsx#L3159-L3196) covers suppressing a redundant confirmation after an attachment. A fix should retain that behavior without hiding a distinct answer or duplicating messages when history is loaded. This report concerns events that reach the WebUI; it does not propose changing the gateway's [separate same-destination message delivery policy](https://github.com/HKUDS/nanobot/blob/37c2af8ffc86c5adf0a9e42732e26722d8a4260b/nanobot/agent/loop.py#L2287-L2292).

**Verification scope:** The results above are from synthetic WebUI tests against the two source revisions. They do not cover a fresh dependency installation, a packaged release, a real gateway or model, image rendering, or a browser reload.

**Workaround:** Request the attachment and the text-only explanation in separate turns. Reloading a thread with the same sequence does not bypass the history projection rule.

prs.body:
---
name: odt
description: "Use this skill whenever the user wants to create, fill, read, or convert OpenDocument Format files (.odt, .ods). Triggers include: any mention of 'ODT', 'ODS', 'ODF', 'OpenDocument', 'LibreOffice document', or requests to produce documents in open-source or ISO standard formats. Also use when converting HTML, Markdown, or TipTap/ProseMirror JSON to ODT, filling ODT templates with data, reading or extracting content from ODT files, generating ODS spreadsheets, reading ODS files, converting XLSX to ODS, converting DOCX to ODT, or creating formal documents like resolutions, reports, letters, contracts, invoices, or memos as .odt files. Use this skill instead of the docx skill when the user explicitly requests .odt output or mentions LibreOffice/OpenOffice as their target application. Do NOT use for .docx files (use the docx skill), PDFs, presentations, or general coding tasks unrelated to document generation."
license: Apache-2.0
---

# odf-kit — OpenDocument Format for JavaScript and TypeScript

## Overview

An `.odt` file is an OpenDocument Format text document — an ISO standard (ISO/IEC 26300) ZIP archive containing XML files. It is the native format for LibreOffice, Apache OpenOffice, Collabora, OnlyOffice, and is supported by Google Docs and Microsoft Office.

odf-kit is the only actively maintained JavaScript/TypeScript library for ODF generation. It produces spec-validated output (validated against the OASIS ODF Validator on every CI run). Works in Node.js 22+ and browsers. No LibreOffice dependency.

## Quick Reference

| Task | Import | Function |
|------|--------|----------|
| Create new ODT document | `"odf-kit"` | `new OdtDocument()` |
| Fill existing ODT template | `"odf-kit"` | `fillTemplate(bytes, data)` |
| HTML → ODT | `"odf-kit"` | `htmlToOdt(html, options?)` |
| Markdown → ODT | `"odf-kit"` | `markdownToOdt(markdown, options?)` |
| TipTap/ProseMirror JSON → ODT | `"odf-kit"` | `tiptapToOdt(json, options?)` |
| Build ODS spreadsheet | `"odf-kit"` | `new OdsDocument()` |
| Read ODT / convert to HTML | `"odf-kit/reader"` | `readOdt(bytes)` / `odtToHtml(bytes)` |
| Read ODS | `"odf-kit/ods-reader"` | `readOds(bytes)` / `odsToHtml(bytes)` |
| XLSX → ODS | `"odf-kit/xlsx"` | `xlsxToOds(bytes)` |
| DOCX → ODT | `"odf-kit/docx"` | `docxToOdt(bytes, options?)` |
| ODT → Typst / PDF | `"odf-kit/typst"` | `odtToTypst(bytes)` |

### Installation

```bash
npm install odf-kit
```

Requires Node.js 22 or later. ESM only.

---

## Creating New ODT Documents

Generate .odt files with JavaScript using odf-kit's builder API.

### Setup

```javascript
import { OdtDocument } from "odf-kit";
import { writeFileSync } from "fs";

const doc = new OdtDocument();
doc.addHeading("Document Title", 1);
doc.addParagraph("Body text goes here.");

const bytes = await doc.save();
writeFileSync("output.odt", bytes);
```

### Metadata

```javascript
doc.setMetadata({
  title: "Quarterly Report",
  creator: "Jane Doe",
  description: "Q4 2026 financial summary",
});
```

### Page Layout

```javascript
doc.setPageLayout({
  orientation: "landscape",       // or "portrait" (default)
  width: "21cm",                  // default A4
  height: "29.7cm",
  marginTop: "2cm",
  marginBottom: "2cm",
  marginLeft: "2cm",
  marginRight: "2cm",
});
```

**For US Letter:** Use `width: "8.5in"` and `height: "11in"`.

### Headers and Footers

```javascript
// Simple string (### = page number)
doc.setHeader("Confidential — Page ###");
doc.setFooter("© 2026 Acme Corp — Page ###");

// Builder for formatted headers
doc.setHeader((h) => {
  h.addText("Confidential", { bold: true, color: "gray" });
  h.addText(" — Page ");
  h.addPageNumber();
});
```

### Headings

```javascript
// Basic heading (levels 1–6)
doc.addHeading("Chapter Title", 1);
doc.addHeading("Section Title", 2);

// With paragraph options
doc.addHeading("Centered Title", 1, { align: "center" });
doc.addHeading("Title with Space", 1, { spaceBefore: "0.5cm", spaceAfter: "0.5cm" });
```

### Paragraphs

```javascript
// Plain text
doc.addParagraph("Simple paragraph.");

// With paragraph options
doc.addParagraph("Right-aligned text.", { align: "right" });

// Builder for mixed formatting
doc.addParagraph((p) => {
  p.addText("Normal and ");
  p.addText("bold", { bold: true });
  p.addText(" text.");
});

// Builder with paragraph options
doc.addParagraph((p) => {
  p.addText("Indented paragraph content.");
}, { indentLeft: "1cm", indentFirst: "0.5cm" });
```

**Paragraph options:**

| Option | Type | Example | Description |
|--------|------|---------|-------------|
| `align` | string | `"left"`, `"center"`, `"right"`, `"justify"` | Text alignment |
| `spaceBefore` | string | `"0.5cm"` | Space above paragraph |
| `spaceAfter` | string | `"0.5cm"` | Space below paragraph |
| `lineHeight` | number or string | `1.5` or `"150%"` | Line spacing (number = multiplier) |
| `indentLeft` | string | `"1cm"` | Left indent |
| `indentRight` | string | `"1cm"` | Right indent |
| `indentFirst` | string | `"0.5cm"` | First-line indent (positive) or hanging indent (negative) |
| `tabStops` | array | `[{ position: "6cm", type: "right" }]` | Tab stop positions |

### Text Formatting

```javascript
doc.addParagraph((p) => {
  p.addText("Bold", { bold: true });
  p.addText("Italic", { italic: true });
  p.addText("Underline", { underline: true });
  p.addText("Strikethrough", { strikethrough: true });
  p.addText("Super", { superscript: true });
  p.addText("Sub", { subscript: true });
  p.addText("Arial 14pt red", { fontFamily: "Arial", fontSize: 14, color: "#CC0000" });
  p.addText("Highlighted", { highlightColor: "#FFFF00" });
  p.addText("UPPERCASE", { textTransform: "uppercase" });
  p.addText("Small Caps", { smallCaps: true });
  p.addText("Weight 300", { fontWeight: 300 });   // numeric 100–900
  p.addText("Weight bold", { fontWeight: "bold" });
});
```

**All text formatting options:**

| Option | Type | Example |
|--------|------|---------|
| `bold` | boolean | `true` |
| `italic` | boolean | `true` |
| `underline` | boolean | `true` |
| `strikethrough` | boolean | `true` |
| `superscript` | boolean | `true` |
| `subscript` | boolean | `true` |
| `fontSize` | number or string | `14` or `"14pt"` |
| `fontFamily` | string | `"Arial"` |
| `fontWeight` | string or number | `"bold"`, `300`, `700` |
| `fontStyle` | string | `"normal"`, `"italic"` |
| `color` | string | `"#FF0000"` or `"red"` |
| `highlightColor` | string | `"#FFFF00"` or `"yellow"` |
| `textTransform` | string | `"uppercase"`, `"lowercase"`, `"capitalize"` |
| `smallCaps` | boolean | `true` |

### Tables

```javascript
// Simple — array of arrays
doc.addTable([
  ["Name", "Role", "Department"],
  ["Alice", "Engineer", "R&D"],
  ["Bob", "Designer", "UX"],
]);

// With options
doc.addTable([
  ["Item", "Price"],
  ["Widget", "$9.99"],
], { columnWidths: ["8cm", "4cm"], border: "0.5pt solid #000000" });

// Full control — builder callback
doc.addTable((t) => {
  t.addRow((r) => {
    r.addCell("Header", {
      bold: true,
      backgroundColor: "#DDDDDD",
      verticalAlign: "middle",
      padding: "0.15cm",
    });
    r.addCell("Value", {
      bold: true,
      backgroundColor: "#DDDDDD",
      colSpan: 2,
    });
  }, { backgroundColor: "#DDDDDD" });

  t.addRow((r) => {
    r.addCell("Status");
    r.addCell("Complete", { color: "green" });
    r.addCell("Verified", { border: "0.5pt solid #000000" });
  });

  // Row spanning
  t.addRow((r) => {
    r.addCell("Tall", { rowSpan: 2, verticalAlign: "top" });
    r.addCell("Normal");
  });
  t.addRow((r) => {
    r.addCell("Adjacent to rowspan");
  });
}, { columnWidths: ["4cm", "4cm", "4cm"] });
```

**Cell options** (extends all text formatting options, plus):

| Option | Type | Example |
|--------|------|---------|
| `backgroundColor` | string | `"#EEEEEE"` |
| `border` | string | `"0.5pt solid #000000"` |
| `borderTop` / `borderBottom` / `borderLeft` / `borderRight` | string | Per-side borders |
| `colSpan` | number | `2` |
| `rowSpan` | number | `3` |
| `verticalAlign` | string | `"top"`, `"middle"`, `"bottom"` |
| `padding` | string | `"0.15cm"` |

### Lists

```javascript
// Simple bullet list
doc.addList(["Apples", "Bananas", "Cherries"]);

// Numbered list
doc.addList(["First", "Second", "Third"], { type: "numbered" });

// Alpha / roman / custom formats
doc.addList(["Item a", "Item b"], { type: "numbered", numFormat: "a" });
doc.addList(["Item A", "Item B"], { type: "numbered", numFormat: "A" });
doc.addList(["Item i", "Item ii"], { type: "numbered", numFormat: "i" });
doc.addList(["Step 5", "Step 6"], { type: "numbered", startValue: 5 });
doc.addList(["Item", "Item"], { type: "numbered", numPrefix: "(", numSuffix: ")" });

// Nested with formatting — builder callback
doc.addList((l) => {
  l.addItem((p) => {
    p.addText("Important: ", { bold: true });
    p.addText("read the documentation");
  });
  l.addItem("Main topic");
  l.addNested((sub) => {
    sub.addItem("Subtopic A");
    sub.addItem("Subtopic B");
  });
});
```

**List options:**

| Option | Type | Example | Description |
|--------|------|---------|-------------|
| `type` | string | `"numbered"` | `"bullet"` (default) or `"numbered"` |
| `numFormat` | string | `"a"`, `"A"`, `"i"`, `"I"` | Number format; default `"1"` |
| `numPrefix` | string | `"("` | Text before number |
| `numSuffix` | string | `")"` | Text after number; default `"."` |
| `startValue` | number | `5` | Starting number |

